  "solution": {
    "text": "As we know that the image of $(1,1)$ with respect to line $x+y+5=0$ is\n$\\frac{x-1}{1}=\\frac{y-1}{1}=\\frac{2(1+1+5)}{1+1}$\n$\\Rightarrow x-1=-7, y-1=-7$\n$\\Rightarrow x=-6, y=-6$\n$\\therefore \\quad$ Image of point $(1,1)$ is $(-6,-6)$ Now, distance from origin\nThis is the required transformed equation.\n$D=\\sqrt{(0+6)^2+(0+6)^2}$\n$D=\\sqrt{72}=6 \\sqrt{2}$",
    "image": null
